  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Joint Global Health Trials Initiative: funding for research calls 1-6</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UK Department of Health and Social Care (DHSC) funds outstanding global health research through the National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR). This programme is administered by the UK Medical Research Council (MRC), which reports activities under the UK Department for Business, Energy and Industrial Strategy (BEIS). NIHR disburses funds to MRC, which makes onwards disbursements to awardees. This activity (Joint Global Health Trials Initiative: funding for research calls 1-6) funds proposals designed to yield implementable results and designed to address the major causes of mortality or morbidity in LMICs. This is a component of Joint Global Health Trials Initiative (GB-GOV-10-JGHT), reported by DHSC.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objectives of this activity are detailed under Joint Global Health Trials Initiative (GB-GOV-10-JGHT), reported by DHSC.</narrative>
  </description>
